{"user": "So it is better to control the corners, what other strategies should I try to implement being behind", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T16:53:40.374397+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 corners are huge because they can\u2019t be flipped back. But when you\u2019re behind in the endgame, also focus on:\n\n- **Mobility:** choose moves that leave White with few legal replies, or force a bad one.\n- **Avoid giving corners:** moves next to corners like **g2** can let White take **h1**.\n- **Stable edges:** edge discs are useful if they don\u2019t hand over a corner.\n- **Endgame counting:** don\u2019t ask \u201chow many do I flip now?\u201d ask \u201cafter White replies, who gets the last empty squares?\u201d\n\nHere, compare your legal moves by White\u2019s reply: **g2** is dangerous because of **h1**; **a7** is an edge move that may limit White more.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T16:53:46.281195+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T16:53:49.093081+00:00", "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Hint": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "llama": ["Think Alo